<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.2.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02101</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.2.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>48780a6b-2fb6-4037-b5d5-f18ba327f2e0</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>The expression \(9t + 7.25\) represents the cost to purchase tickets for a concert, where \(t\) is the number of tickets. A group of friends paid $79.25 for tickets. How many tickets were bought?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 6 tickets </item>
  <item> 8 tickets </item>
  <item> 10 tickets </item>
  <item> 12 tickets </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 8 tickets</para>
<para>Use the following to answer questions 2–4.</para>
<para>A model rocket is launched from a launchpad. The function modeling the height of the rocket, in feet, \(t\) seconds after being launched is shown.</para>
<para>\(f(t) = -15t^2 + 58t + 8\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which equation would you solve to find the time at which the rocket hits the ground?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(-15t^2 + 58t + 8 = 0\) </item>
  <item> \(-15t^2 + 58t = 8\) </item>
  <item> \(-15t^2 + 58t = 0\) </item>
  <item> \(15t^2 + 58t + 8 = 0\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(-15t^2 + 58t + 8 = 0\) </para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Use a non-graphing method to find the solution to the previous equation to determine the time that has passed when the rocket hits the ground.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 2 seconds </item>
  <item> 3 seconds </item>
  <item> 4 seconds </item>
  <item> 5 seconds </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 4 seconds</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>How high off the ground is the launchpad from which the rocket lifts off?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 0 feet </item>
  <item> 2 feet </item>
  <item> 8 feet </item>
  <item> 15 feet </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 8 feet</para>
<para>Use the following to answer questions 5–8.</para>
<para>The expressions \(t(90 − 3t)\) and \(-3t^2 + 90t\) define the same function. The function models the number of lumens emitted by a spotlight in an art exhibit over the course of \(t\) seconds.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which equation represents the time when the spotlight is not emitting any light?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> \(t(90 − 3t) = -3t^2 + 90t\) </item>
  <item> \(-3t^2 + 90t = 675\) </item>
  <item> \(-3t^2 + 90t = 0\) </item>
  <item> \(-3t^2 + 90t = 30\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(-3t^2 + 90t = 0\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>At what time(s) does the spotlight not emit any light?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 0 and 30 seconds </item>
  <item> 10 and 25 seconds </item>
  <item>Only 0 seconds </item>
  <item> 15 seconds </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 0 and 30 seconds</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>The artist planned for the spotlight to emit 600 lumens at 10 seconds from the start. At what other time will the spotlight emit 600 lumens of light?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 0 seconds </item>
  <item> 20 seconds </item>
  <item> 25 seconds </item>
  <item> 30 seconds </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 20 seconds</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>At 5 seconds, the spotlight will emit 375 lumens. Find another time that the spotlight emits 375 lumens.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 0 seconds </item>
  <item> 10 seconds </item>
  <item> 15 seconds </item>
  <item> 25 seconds </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 25 seconds</para>
<para>Use the following to answer questions 9 and 10.</para>
<para>A bowling alley models the revenue from sales in one day as a function of the cost to rent a lane per hour, \(c\). Here are two expressions defining the same revenue function.</para>
<para>\(c(160 − 10c)\)</para>
<para>\(160c − 10^2\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>According to this model, how high would the cost to rent a lane have to be for the bowling alley to make $0 in revenue?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> $8 </item>
  <item> $10 </item>
  <item> $14 </item>
  <item> $16 </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> $16</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item> What equation can you write to determine the lane cost that would allow the bowling alley to make $640 in revenue?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item>\( c(160 − 10c) = 0\) </item>
  <item>\( c(160 − 10c) = 640\) </item>
  <item>\( 160c − 10c^2 + 640 = 0\) </item>
  <item>\( 160c − 10c^2 = 0\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(c(160 − 10c) = 640\)</para></section>
